{
  "abstract": "The complementary curve $C_F$ in Lasić and Oblak’s Croatian construction supplies seven rational entries with nineteen specified square products plus one. We prove that every specialization with distinct nonzero entries has exactly nineteen such squares: neither of the remaining two conditions can hold. A compact chart reduces one missing condition to the genus-seven curve $\\eta^2=k^4-17k^2+25$, $p^2=4k^6-8k^4-140k^2+225$. Its complete rational-point list has $k=0,\\pm1,\\pm4,\\pm5/4$, giving twenty-eight affine points and four rational points at infinity. Every finite point lies at a pole or a zero/collision boundary of the entry chart. Reciprocity exchanges the two missing conditions. For completeness, we descend a rank-two rational elliptic curve to four classes over a cubic field and choose between two necessary elliptic covers in each class. Retaining the original square condition $x=4k^2$ lowers a blocking rank-three cover to rank one; the four chosen covers have ranks two, zero, two and one. Certified elliptic Chabauty computations then finish the point decision. An independent finite-field argument supplies exactly the saturation required in the nontrivial rank-two case. The supplement includes all nineteen literal roots, exact source and inverse maps, independent symbolic and rational checks, and warning-free arithmetic certificates. This excludes only the specified complementary curve; the Konavle curve, the larger two-parameter surface, and the rational septuple problem remain unresolved.",
